   "Three schemas: internal (storage), conceptual (logical structure), external (per-group views).",
   "Physical data independence: storage changes do not reach applications (internal/conceptual mapping absorbs them).",
   "Logical data independence: conceptual growth does not break external views (external/conceptual mapping absorbs it).",
   "A DBMS centralises definition (DDL), constraints, transactions and recovery."
