     "File system, physical change: every program that reads the student file knows the record layout and scan pattern; reorganisation and the new field alter offsets - expect edits in admissions, fees and library programs, plus re-testing each.",
     "File system, logical change: adding email changes the record format read by all programs - again, all of them need recompilation and many need code changes.",
     "DBMS, physical change: the DBA swaps the storage structure and updates the internal/conceptual mapping. Conceptual schema, views and applications: untouched. This is physical data independence.",
     "DBMS, logical change: email is added to the conceptual schema. Existing external views do not include it, so their mapping simply ignores it; only applications that want email change. This is logical data independence."
